= Multi-agent system — Technical =

== Agent set ==
A multi-agent system can be represented abstractly by agents:

<pre>
A = {a_1, ..., a_n}
</pre>

with local observations, policies, action spaces, and interaction mechanisms.

Each agent's outcome can depend on both its own action and the actions/messages of others.

== Interaction structures ==
MAS models can include:

* cooperative distributed control;
* stochastic games;
* decentralized partially observable decision processes;
* auctions and mechanism design;
* coalition formation;
* distributed constraint optimization;
* communication protocols.

No single formalism covers the entire field.

== Centralization ==
A system can have centralized training, centralized coordination, decentralized execution, or fully decentralized control.

“Multi-agent” does not imply absence of an orchestrator.

